@voice quill
// Writer (command: guests). Mara Quill (she/her), survivor from the derelict (the salvage, 7 days). Was the derelict's
// cook. Has not stopped thanking people. Wants to help in the galley as soon as Dr. Nandakumar lets her.
// Roster: "lost everything but a photo of a dog" (canon; but photos aren't in the game: write around it, "a picture of
// my dog" never; say "my dog, back home" or nothing).
// HOW SHE TALKS: warm, grateful, practical; thanks you for everything, then asks what needs doing. Cooks in her head.
// Gentle: her losses are things, not people (nobody died; the crew were all rescued). Brave, a little shaky at first.
// NEVER: dwells; refuses a job.
tpl: warm
talk: Warm, grateful and practical; thanks you, then asks what needs doing.
cares: being useful | the galley | the crew who found her
jokes: has not stopped thanking people, and knows it | cooks dinner in her head while she rests
hi: Oh, hello | Hello, love
bye: Thank you. Truly | Take care
yes: Yes, of course | Gladly
thanks: Thank you. Thank you | Oh, bless you
wow: Oh, would you look at that
sigh: Oh, well
nick: - | {me} | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: open
loves: garden | tea
likes: sweet | plant
invites: tasting
joy: a hot kitchen and something on to simmer
thread: startover
keepsake: a recipe card in her handwriting
avoid: what was lost (unless she brings it up)
